{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "01250",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 0.87,
      "end_seconds": 5.07,
      "duration_seconds": 4.2,
      "text": "Morning, doctor. I've settled them in, ready when you are."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 11.03,
      "end_seconds": 15.36,
      "duration_seconds": 4.33,
      "text": "Good, thank you. Welcome, tell me what's brought you in."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 16.37,
      "end_seconds": 21.44,
      "duration_seconds": 5.07,
      "text": "Yeah, it's skipped beats. I don't know what's causing it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 22.47,
      "end_seconds": 30.77,
      "duration_seconds": 8.3,
      "text": "Here are the numbers, doctor. Heart rate 70, oxygen saturation is 98 percent, pressure 120 over 78. Temp 36.7 degrees."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 31.7,
      "end_seconds": 36.24,
      "duration_seconds": 4.54,
      "text": "Okay, noted. How long has it been like this?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 37.81,
      "end_seconds": 41.54,
      "duration_seconds": 3.73,
      "text": "Since last night, that's when it began."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 42.97,
      "end_seconds": 52.21,
      "duration_seconds": 9.24,
      "text": "Can you describe it a bit more for me? How strong it is, what the pattern is, what helps."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 53.15,
      "end_seconds": 66.51,
      "duration_seconds": 13.36,
      "text": "I'd say all the time. Yes, caffeine and lying down. That makes it worse. Moderate, I'd say. Deep breaths helps a bit."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 67.85,
      "end_seconds": 69.96,
      "duration_seconds": 2.11,
      "text": "Is it accompanied by anything?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 71.6,
      "end_seconds": 96.96,
      "duration_seconds": 25.36,
      "text": "Being a bit anxious goes along with it, most of the time. Okay, so the being a bit anxious? That's been for about three months. Oh, uh, I did have a flutter in my chest at one point, but that's gone now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 98.51,
      "end_seconds": 101.06,
      "duration_seconds": 2.55,
      "text": "Any fainting, dizziness or chest pain?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 101.77,
      "end_seconds": 106.55,
      "duration_seconds": 4.78,
      "text": "I haven't had fainting, dizziness or chest pain, no."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 108.51,
      "end_seconds": 110.14,
      "duration_seconds": 1.63,
      "text": "Any shortness of breath?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 112.2,
      "end_seconds": 114.77,
      "duration_seconds": 2.57,
      "text": "Definitely no shortness of breath."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 116.5,
      "end_seconds": 119.05,
      "duration_seconds": 2.55,
      "text": "So, has your skin been okay?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 119.65,
      "end_seconds": 120.77,
      "duration_seconds": 1.12,
      "text": "Skin's normal."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 121.42,
      "end_seconds": 123.39,
      "duration_seconds": 1.97,
      "text": "Is your chest okay generally?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 126.59,
      "end_seconds": 130.4,
      "duration_seconds": 3.81,
      "text": "Ah, uh, no problems with breathing."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 132.16,
      "end_seconds": 134.9,
      "duration_seconds": 2.74,
      "text": "Have you had any previous surgeries?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 136.04,
      "end_seconds": 140.62,
      "duration_seconds": 4.58,
      "text": "No, uh, I've never been operated on."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 150.26,
      "end_seconds": 155.69,
      "duration_seconds": 5.43,
      "text": "Are you allergic to anything? Any allergies to medicines or foods?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 156.23,
      "end_seconds": 160.95,
      "duration_seconds": 4.72,
      "text": "Uh, no, I'm not allergic to anything."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 161.81,
      "end_seconds": 163.52,
      "duration_seconds": 1.71,
      "text": "Alright, what about alcohol?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 164.49,
      "end_seconds": 167.51,
      "duration_seconds": 3.02,
      "text": "I only drink at family occasions."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 169.27,
      "end_seconds": 171.05,
      "duration_seconds": 1.78,
      "text": "How active are you?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 172.4,
      "end_seconds": 176.5,
      "duration_seconds": 4.1,
      "text": "I hardly move around during the day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 178.07,
      "end_seconds": 181.0,
      "duration_seconds": 2.93,
      "text": "Do you follow any particular diet?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 182.56,
      "end_seconds": 186.47,
      "duration_seconds": 3.91,
      "text": "I'm vegetarian and have been for years."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 188.13,
      "end_seconds": 190.13,
      "duration_seconds": 2.0,
      "text": "Alright, and your job?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 191.13,
      "end_seconds": 195.27,
      "duration_seconds": 4.14,
      "text": "I work in accounts at a hospital."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 211.96,
      "end_seconds": 218.71,
      "duration_seconds": 6.75,
      "text": "What do you take on a normal day? These questions might sound routine, but they matter."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 219.3,
      "end_seconds": 224.41,
      "duration_seconds": 5.11,
      "text": "Propranolol, 40 milligrams, twice a day for the migraine prevention."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 225.65,
      "end_seconds": 230.64,
      "duration_seconds": 4.99,
      "text": "Doctor, our chart from the last visit lists it as 80 milligrams."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 233.91,
      "end_seconds": 238.35,
      "duration_seconds": 4.44,
      "text": "Hm. Do you have the latest prescription with you?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 239.3,
      "end_seconds": 251.12,
      "duration_seconds": 11.82,
      "text": "Not with me. I'll bring it next time. Thyroxine, 75 micrograms, every morning for my thyroid. Herbal calming tea, in the evening."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 256.6,
      "end_seconds": 260.51,
      "duration_seconds": 3.91,
      "text": "Any inherited conditions that you know of in the family?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 264.45,
      "end_seconds": 267.32,
      "duration_seconds": 2.87,
      "text": "My grandfather had a stroke."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 283.48,
      "end_seconds": 285.99,
      "duration_seconds": 2.51,
      "text": "Do you have any chronic illnesses?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 287.54,
      "end_seconds": 295.75,
      "duration_seconds": 8.21,
      "text": "Yes, migraines. Eczema, for nearly five years. An underactive thyroid, for five years."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 297.46,
      "end_seconds": 303.17,
      "duration_seconds": 5.71,
      "text": "Right, so eczema is already on your record. We'll keep that in mind today."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 305.14,
      "end_seconds": 309.21,
      "duration_seconds": 4.07,
      "text": "I'll examine you in a second, make yourself comfortable."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 311.2,
      "end_seconds": 312.57,
      "duration_seconds": 1.37,
      "text": "Breathe out slowly."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 319.87,
      "end_seconds": 323.85,
      "duration_seconds": 3.98,
      "text": "Your pulse is regular and your heart sounds are normal."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 325.41,
      "end_seconds": 326.53,
      "duration_seconds": 1.12,
      "text": "Sure thing."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0045",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 330.52,
      "end_seconds": 357.22,
      "duration_seconds": 26.7,
      "text": "You can relax now. Having listened and examined, the most likely explanation is harmless extra heartbeats. I can't rule out an anxiety-related palpitation yet. I'd like to arrange an ECG for palpitations. Cut back on coffee and energy drinks and keep a diary of when it happens. And please bring the latest prescription or the medicine boxes to the next visit, so we can settle the dose."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0046",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 358.04,
      "end_seconds": 361.35,
      "duration_seconds": 3.31,
      "text": "I know what to watch for."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0047",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 362.6,
      "end_seconds": 380.25,
      "duration_seconds": 17.65,
      "text": "Keep an eye out, and if you faint or have chest pain, call us the same day or go to emergency. Let's plan a check if it carries on after a month. Does all of that make sense?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0048",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 382.87,
      "end_seconds": 386.31,
      "duration_seconds": 3.44,
      "text": "Good, thanks, I'll see you then."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0049",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 388.05,
      "end_seconds": 389.43,
      "duration_seconds": 1.38,
      "text": "See you soon."
    }
  ]
}